# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in its system config, which rewrites
# the LF blobs in this repository to CRLF on checkout. `npm pack` copies the
# working tree rather than the committed blobs, so that CRLF reached the
# published tarball and left scripts/install.sh unrunnable by /bin/sh on Linux
# and macOS. Attributes take precedence over core.autocrlf, so pin the working
# tree to LF on every platform.
#
# This only changes checkout. Every blob is already LF, so the raw
# githubusercontent.com URLs used by the `curl | sh` and `irm | iex` installers
# serve exactly the same bytes as before.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts are covered by the rule above on purpose: the LF blob is
# what the `irm | iex` installer already serves and runs in production. If a
# Windows tool ever needs CRLF on disk, add `*.ps1 text eol=crlf` here, which
# likewise changes only the checkout and never the stored blob.

# Future-proofing; no binary files are tracked today.
*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.tgz binary
*.gz binary
